---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import ControllerIdentity from '../components/privacy/ControllerIdentity.astro';
import ChildrensPrivacy from '../components/privacy/ChildrensPrivacy.astro';
import PrivacyContact from '../components/privacy/PrivacyContact.astro';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How GLANCE Apps handles your data. Short version: we don't collect it."
  lastUpdated="October 16, 2026"
>
  <p class="lead">
    Short version: GLANCE Apps does not collect, store, or share your personal
    data. Your information stays on your device.
  </p>

  <ControllerIdentity>
    <p>
      This privacy policy covers our publisher-level practices and the
      glance-apps.com website. Each app may have additional privacy details
      specific to its features; see the privacy policy linked from each app's
      product page. lastGLANCE's details are in the{' '}
      <a href="#lastglance">lastGLANCE section</a> below.
    </p>
  </ControllerIdentity>

  <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    All content you create within our Apps is stored locally on your device
    using your platform's standard on-device storage. This data remains under
    your control at all times.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you use your platform's automatic backup service (iCloud Backup, Google
    Backup, or similar), your device data may be backed up as part of your
    standard device backup. This is governed by your platform provider's privacy
    policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Optional cloud sync</h2>
  <p>
    Some Apps offer optional cloud sync to a destination you control, such as
    WebDAV, Nextcloud, a self-hosted GLANCEvault instance, iCloud Drive, or a
    folder that a sync tool you already use keeps in step across your devices.
    GLANCE Apps does not operate any of these sync servers.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you sync to a GLANCEvault instance you host, your data is always
    encrypted client-side before leaving your device; the server stores encrypted
    content and never has access to your item contents or your passphrase. When
    you sync to WebDAV or Nextcloud, client-side encryption is optional and off by
    default; enable each app's sync-encryption option to encrypt your data before
    upload. When you sync to iCloud Drive, your data is stored in your personal
    iCloud account under Apple's standard encryption, governed by Apple's privacy
    policy. See each app's privacy policy for the details of its encryption model.
  </p>
  <p>
    Sync is off by default.
  </p>

  <h2>Per-app integrations</h2>
  <p>
    Some Apps offer optional integrations that let applications or services you
    choose read data the App manages, such as dayGLANCE's local MCP server for
    AI assistants. Anything those third parties receive is governed by their
    policies, not ours, and the exposure is a consequence of your choice to
    connect them. Every such integration is off by default and described in
    detail in the relevant app's privacy policy, linked from each app's product
    page.
  </p>

  <h2 id="lastglance">lastGLANCE</h2>
  <p>
    lastGLANCE tracks when you last did recurring chores and, with People, when
    you were last in touch with the people who matter to you. Everything you
    enter (chores, completions, people, their dates, logged contacts and notes)
    is stored on your device. This section describes what lastGLANCE accesses
    and where your data can go. Every feature below is optional, and nothing
    reaches GLANCE Apps.
  </p>

  <h3>Phone contacts (People)</h3>
  <p>
    On Android and iOS, lastGLANCE can read your phone's contacts to import people
    or link a person to a contact. This is off by default. lastGLANCE asks for
    contacts permission only after you turn on Phone contacts in Settings and
    confirm an in-app explanation, and you can turn it off or revoke the
    permission at any time. Access is read-only: lastGLANCE never adds, changes,
    or deletes your contacts.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      When you import, lastGLANCE saves the contacts you choose as people, with
      their names and dates (such as birthdays), in the app's local storage.
    </li>
    <li>
      When you link a person to a contact, lastGLANCE remembers which contact it
      is on that device only. The link is not synced.
    </li>
    <li>
      Phone numbers and email addresses are read at the moment you tap Call, Text
      or Email, and a contact photo when you open the person. They are handed to
      your phone's dialer, messaging or mail app, or shown on screen, and are not
      stored by lastGLANCE.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Imported people leave your device only if you turn on sync, as described
    below.
  </p>

  <h3>Sync</h3>
  <p>
    lastGLANCE can sync to destinations you configure: a WebDAV server (such as
    Nextcloud), a GLANCEvault instance, or a folder that a sync tool you choose
    (such as Syncthing, Nextcloud, Google Drive, Dropbox, OneDrive or
    FolderSync) keeps in step across your devices. Sync is off by default. Your
    People data travels as its own file or vault collection, alongside your
    chores, and uses the same encryption as your chores.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      GLANCEvault: your data is always encrypted on your device before it is
      sent. The server stores encrypted content only.
    </li>
    <li>
      WebDAV: encryption is optional and off by default. Turn it on in Cloud Sync
      to encrypt your data before upload. Otherwise it is stored on your server
      as plain text, protected by that server's own access controls.
    </li>
    <li>
      Folder sync: encryption is a per-device switch in Cloud Sync. The file is
      stored wherever your sync tool keeps that folder and is governed by that
      tool's privacy policy.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your encryption passphrase is never stored. The key derived from it is kept
    on your device (in the Android Keystore on Android) so you are not asked for
    it on every launch. If you forget your passphrase, encrypted data cannot be
    recovered.
  </p>
  <p>
    Household: if you share lastGLANCE with your household, the members' display
    names are kept in a small shared file on your sync destination so other GLANCE
    Apps can recognize the same people. This file is not encrypted. It stays on
    the destination you control.
  </p>
  <p>
    The web version of lastGLANCE may relay WebDAV requests through a stateless
    proxy we host, because browsers block many direct requests. Your server
    address, credentials and data pass through it in transit and are never stored
    or logged. The Android and iOS apps connect to your server directly.
  </p>

  <h3>Connections to other GLANCE Apps and automation</h3>
  <p>
    These are off by default, and each one runs only through the sync
    destinations you set up for it. They send nothing to GLANCE Apps.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      dayGLANCE: lastGLANCE can send chores, a reminder to get in touch with
      someone whose catch-up is overdue, and today's birthdays and other dates to
      dayGLANCE as tasks, and receive completions back.
    </li>
    <li>
      lifeGLANCE: for people you choose, lastGLANCE can add each contact you log
      to your lifeGLANCE timeline.
    </li>
    <li>
      Automation apps such as Tasker (Android): other apps on your phone can ask
      lastGLANCE to add or complete a chore, log a contact or open a screen, and
      read summary counts such as how many chores are overdue.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These messages use the GLANCEintents protocol and can be encrypted with your
    sync passphrase.
  </p>

  <h3>Notifications and widgets</h3>
  <p>
    Chore reminders, date reminders and the daily catch-up digest are scheduled
    on your device. Home screen and Lock Screen widgets read a summary of your
    chores and people (names, how long since you were in touch, upcoming dates)
    that the app saves on your device. None of this is sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <h3>Purchases</h3>
  <p>
    The Google Play version offers an optional unlock, processed entirely by
    Google Play. We do not see or store your payment information. Purchase status
    is checked on your device through Google Play and is not sent to us. Google's
    privacy policy governs payment processing.
  </p>

  <h2>Data we do not collect</h2>
  <p>
    Our Apps are designed to operate entirely on your device. We do not:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Require you to create an account</li>
    <li>Collect personally identifiable information</li>
    <li>Store your notes, entries, or any app content on any servers we control (the web versions of some Apps route sync traffic through a stateless relay we host, in transit only and never stored; see each app's privacy policy)</li>
    <li>Track your location</li>
    <li>Use advertising identifiers</li>
    <li>Sell or share your data with third parties</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We do not use third-party analytics services. Your platform's distribution
    service (such as Apple's App Store Connect or Google Play Console) may share
    aggregated, anonymized crash and usage data with us if you have opted into
    analytics on your device. This data cannot be used to identify you individually.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    The glance-apps.com website is a static site served via Vercel. Vercel may
    collect standard web server logs (IP address, request times, page URLs) for
    operational purposes. We do not use cookies, tracking pixels, or analytics
    scripts on this site.
  </p>

  <ChildrensPrivacy />

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we make material changes to this policy, we will update the "Last updated"
    date at the top of this page and notify users through the Apps or this website
    before changes take effect.
  </p>

  <PrivacyContact />
</ProseLayout>
